// ------------------------------------------------------------------ Chapter 5
const chapter5 = [
  h1("Chapter 5—Discussion and Conclusions"),
  h2("5.1 Research Hypotheses Findings"),
  body("**RQ1 / H1′.** The choice between event time and processing time is immaterial at a five-minute sampling cadence: the 1.4 s mean lag changes the label of two events in twelve thousand and costs nothing in ranking quality. What matters is alignment error at the scale of the window: in the paired comparison on frozen labels the best cyber model loses 0.033 AUPRC at 120 s (the pre-registered rule, which requires every seed's interval above zero, is not met at this level) and 0.129 at 300 s (met), and coupled physical evidence compensates for part of that loss. The framework's timestamp requirement is therefore a bound on alignment error relative to the window, not a preference for one timestamp field."),
  body("**RQ2 / H2′.** On a target that is not saturated, the trained relational model showed a positive mean advantage over the sequential model at both coupling levels (seed-level p ≈ 0.02), but H2′ is not supported under its pre-registered rule: the κ = 1 mean (0.029) is below the 0.03 margin, only five of ten seeds' cluster intervals exclude zero at each level, and three seeds at each level favour the Transformer by point estimate. The defensible statement is that the relational model is more often better, by an amount whose seed-level interval is 0.01 to 0.12 at κ = 0 and 0.01 to 0.05 at κ = 1, and that a larger seed count would be needed to establish the margin. The earlier verdict that the R-GCN was inferior—reported in every prior version of this praxis—was an artifact of a training budget capped at 50 gradient steps."),
  body("**RQ3 / H3′, H4, H5.** Lag-weighted relations add nothing measurable; the relations together with the flow-level evidence they carry add 0.064 AUPRC where no physical coupling exists (p = 0.008) and 0.021 where it does. H5 is not supported as pre-registered: at zero jitter no coupling level met the criterion against the validation-selected unimodal comparator, although late fusion showed positive mean gains of +0.086 at κ = 0.5 and +0.140 at κ = 0.75, and at κ = 1 the physical model alone is best. Under nonzero jitter 5 conditions met the rule (three for late-fusion RF at κ = 0.5, two for logistic fusion at κ = 1 and σ = 300 s); these are exploratory. Relative to the cyber-only model, the operationally relevant reference, late fusion detects coupling from a rank correlation of about 0.75, concatenation fusion only at 1.0, and linear fusion never within the window scale. Below those strengths an honest null is the expected result of this framework, and the praxis reports one."),
  h2("5.2 Conclusions"),
  body("Five conclusions are supported. First, source-level partition disjointness is necessary but not sufficient: the v2 replay passed 34 leakage checks and still delivered a held-out label identical to the capture session. Evaluation must test what a shortcut could exploit—session, flow presence, prevalence—with a required margin, not only whether observations are shared. Second, the benchmark's native attack-window label is a regime label at the window scale, separable by destination-host diversity; results on it calibrate a pipeline and say nothing about model families. Third, the fusion question can be given content without coincident data by injecting coupling of known strength, provided the comparator and the jitter condition are stated with the floor: against the cyber-only model at zero jitter the floor is ρ ≈ 0.75 for late fusion; against the validation-selected unimodal model no zero-jitter level met the rule. Fourth, a model comparison is only as valid as the weakest training protocol it contains; the largest single effect in this study (+0.21 AUPRC) came from allowing one model to train to convergence. Fifth, once trained, relational modeling of flow evidence is more often better than sequential modeling on the same inputs, with an advantage attributable to the relations and the flow-level evidence they carry; the pre-registered margin was not established. None of this is evidence of cyber-physical incidents near PANC; the aircraft and cyber records remain independent by construction."),
  h2("5.3 Contributions to the Body of Knowledge"),
  ...numbered([
    "A leakage-audited alignment method for pairing sparse event streams with dense telemetry: regime-stratified, embargoed source blocks with gates for reuse, overlap, class composition, and session confounding, and an independent validator. The method generalizes to any replay of one time series onto another.",
    "A documented three-stage validity correction (source reuse, session confound, ceiling target) with the artifacts to verify each stage, offered as a case study in self-auditing evaluation for cyber-physical analytics.",
    "A parametric coupling-injection protocol that turns an unanswerable fusion question into a measurable one, with attribution tracking as a ground-truth test of the tabular explanation layer and detection floors stated per comparator and jitter condition.",
    "Cluster-corrected inference for replayed evaluations: non-overlapping source bins, design effects of 19–30, and effective samples of roughly 60–100 where nominal samples were 1,828.",
    "Evidence, with ten seeds and paired cluster intervals, that a trained relational graph model holds a positive mean advantage over a temporal Transformer on a graded attack-intensity target—short of the pre-registered acceptance rule—and that the advantage is attributable to relations and the flow-level evidence they carry rather than to lag weighting; and the finding that the earlier contrary result was a training-protocol artifact.",
    "A reproducible artifact package (595 files, checksummed) with the position bank, coupling grid, patched notebook, and aggregation scripts needed to extend every experiment.",
  ]),
  h2("5.4 Limitations"),
  body("The benchmark provides two capture sessions and three window-scale regimes, so held-out information is bounded at 27–49 independent windows regardless of event count, and Session 2 can never supply benign windows. Coupling is synthetic; the anomaly score is a transparent composite chosen for testability rather than operational realism. The trained R-GCN, while better than the Transformer, remains below a regularized logistic regression at κ = 0 and below late fusion at κ = 1, and both neural models appear to pay for uninformative physical inputs. The Transformer was not retrained under an equivalently generous budget; its mini-batch schedule already provided roughly 1,200 steps, but a matched-budget comparison would strengthen H2′. Latency comparisons across model families were made on different hardware. Explanation quality was validated on the final checkpoints of three representative runs (single seed each, 96-event evaluation subset) and against injected ground truth at the tabular level; the Transformer's attribution failed fidelity at κ = 0, flow-level attributions were unstable, and no validation involved operators."),
  h2("5.5 Recommendations for Future Research"),
  ...numbered([
    "Matched-budget and cyber-only neural variants: retrain the Transformer with early stopping on a budget equivalent to the corrected R-GCN, and add modality-gated or cyber-only variants of both to test whether the gap to the linear model is the cost of noise features.",
    "Seed-count closure for H2′: at ten seeds the margin test has p = 0.09 at κ = 0; twenty seeds at the two κ levels are inexpensive and would settle whether the advantage reaches 0.03.",
    "Late-fusion and stacked heads for the neural models, following the tabular finding that concatenation dilutes coupled physical evidence by 0.13 AUPRC.",
    "A finer cyber target—attack category composition or per-category intensity within plateaus—to raise the number of independent labeled regimes beyond three.",
    "Coincident data: a NetFlow capture from the same period and site as the aircraft observations, with clearance, which would replace injected coupling with observed coupling and make the detection floor an operational statement.",
    "An operator study of the analyst evidence cards, outside the present IRB-free boundary, to test whether validated attribution improves triage decisions.",
  ]),
  h2("5.6 Closing Statement"),
  body("The praxis set out to show when combining aircraft observations with network telemetry improves prioritization of low-altitude events near critical infrastructure, and to state the limits of that evidence. It found that the limits are where the value is: the framework cannot manufacture coupling that the data do not contain, but it can detect coupling above a stated strength, resist the shortcuts that made earlier results look better than they were, explain what it relies on, and correct its own comparisons when a protocol proves inadequate. That is the practical resolution this D.Eng. praxis offers to the operator who must decide, in real time and with imperfect alignment, whether two independent streams of evidence are telling one story."),
];

